{#
  Container: enforces the 1120px measure and the gutter.

  Page rhythm is not something builders re-apply by hand. Reach for section()
  first, which already applies this; use container() bare only when you need
  the measure without the 96px vertical rhythm (inside the masthead, say).

  Emits .cs-container, never max-w-main plus px-8. That spelling was rejected
  and the reason is in components/container.css.

  Usage:
    {% raw %}{% from "components/container.njk" import container %}
    {% call container() %}...{% endcall %}{% endraw %}
#}
{#- `orient` names this block for the masthead's left slot. It emits a
    data-orient attribute on the container that already exists, so naming a
    section costs no element and no wrapper. main.js caches each one's top and
    writes the name of whichever is under the bar. Omit it and the block is not
    a section as far as the header is concerned. -#}
{% macro container(class="", narrow=false, orient="") %}
<div class="cs-container{{ " cs-container--narrow" if narrow }}{{ " " + class if class }}"{% if orient %} data-orient="{{ orient }}"{% endif %}>
  {{ caller() }}
</div>
{% endmacro %}
